### 38. `tsl/src/compression/compression_dml.c:78` - `TupleDescGetAttrNumber` - Missing return on not found

**Defect at line 84:** Function returns `InvalidAttrNumber` if not found. But the loop at line 81 returns on match. If not found, falls through to line 84. But wait, the function declaration says `static inline int TupleDescGetAttrNumber(TupleDesc desc, const char *name)`. It returns `int` but `AttrNumber` is `int16`. Return type mismatch but C allows it.

**Real defect:** The function has no explicit return after the loop! At line 84: `return InvalidAttrNumber;` — but this is OUTSIDE the function! Look at the diff:
```c
 static inline int TupleDescGetAttrNumber(TupleDesc desc, const char *name)
 {
 	for (int i = 0; i < desc->natts; i++)
 	{
 		if (strcmp(name, NameStr(desc->attrs[i].attname)) == 0)
 			return desc->attrs[i].attnum;
 	}
+
 	return InvalidAttrNumber;
 }
```
The `+` line is the added blank line. The `return InvalidAttrNumber;` is at the same indentation as the function body. In the old code (not shown), it might have been missing! The diff shows the function previously didn't have a return for not-found case (falling off end → undefined behavior). The new code ADDS the return. This is a **BUG FIX**, not a defect.

